custom-blocklist-heading = Your additional blocked hosts
mandatory = Mandatory
adjustable = User adjustable
add-host-label = Block host:
add-host-button = Add blocked host
remove-host-button = Remove
custom-blocklist-empty = No additional blocked hosts.
custom-blocklist-match = Applied at URL and download review. A host also blocks its dot-boundary subdomains, ignoring case; a similarly named domain is not blocked. Enter a hostname, not a URL or wildcard.
custom-phrases-heading = Your additional blocked HTML-text phrases
add-phrase-label = Block HTML text:
add-phrase-button = Add blocked phrase
remove-phrase-button = Remove
custom-phrases-empty = No additional blocked phrases.
custom-phrases-match = Applied before page parsing. Phrases match text between HTML tags, including hidden or script text, ignoring case and normalizing whitespace.
custom-extensions-heading = Your additional blocked download extensions
add-extension-label = Block file extension (for example .zip):
add-extension-button = Add blocked extension
remove-extension-button = Remove
custom-extensions-empty = No additional blocked download extensions.
custom-extensions-match = Applied before download bytes begin. File-name suffixes match without case sensitivity.
custom-popup-phrases-heading = Your additional blocked extension-popup phrases
add-popup-phrase-label = Block popup text:
add-popup-phrase-button = Add blocked popup phrase
remove-popup-phrase-button = Remove
custom-popup-phrases-empty = No additional blocked popup phrases.
custom-popup-phrases-match = Applied before an extension's native popup appears. Phrases match the reviewed popup metadata without case sensitivity and with normalized whitespace.
locked-note = Safety floor: every listed baseline rule and workflow step is enforced by the gatekeeper process. User settings can only add protection.
unavailable = The AI gatekeeper is unavailable, so its settings cannot be read or changed right now.
saved = Gatekeeper settings saved.
invalid = The requested gatekeeper settings change was rejected.
